/home/runner/work/_temp/shurik-runtime-MnTPKq/source/ARCHITECTURE.md:44:[Pi AI's provider layer](https://github.com/earendil-works/pi/blob/main/packages/ai/README.md#providers-and-models) supports individual provider factories or a collection of all built-in providers. Its [authentication layer](https://github.com/earendil-works/pi/blob/main/packages/ai/README.md#auth) resolves provider credentials from supported environment variables, credential stores, OAuth, or ambient cloud configuration. Custom compatible endpoints require a registered custom provider with its own model metadata and authentication.
/home/runner/work/_temp/shurik-runtime-MnTPKq/source/ARCHITECTURE.md:52:The iteration action inherits native provider environment variables and cloud configuration. Pi AI resolves authentication; Shurik supplies no per-request API-key override, interactive login flow, or persistent credential store. The existing `opencode-api-key` input remains an optional environment alias. Credentials never become action configuration, worker-request JSON, or saved control fields. Publication redaction includes provider key/token variables and cloud credentials present in the environment. Bundled metadata comes from the installed Pi AI package; unlisted IDs use provisional metadata. Additional custom endpoints need an adapter integration.
/home/runner/work/_temp/shurik-runtime-MnTPKq/source/ARCHITECTURE.md:142:The worker shares the Actions runner and job credentials. Separate checkouts isolate engine selection from task files operationally; they are not a security sandbox. Sessions follow the consumer repository's visibility. Redaction reduces accidental credential publication, with the limits documented in [README.md](README.md#caveats).
